al guidelines.\n\n**Recommendations:**  \n\n- **Immediate actions**  \n  - Apply water so that the soil receives a depth of **7–8 cm** in each irrigation event.\n\n- **Monitoring advice**  \n  - After irrigation, observe the soil‑moisture sensor to confirm that moisture has increased appropriately.  \n  - Keep an eye on leaf colour and turgor; normal green, firm leaves suggest adequate water.\n\n- **When to seek expert help**  \n  - If soil‑moisture readings stay unusually low or high despite applying the recommended depth.  \n  - If the crop shows persistent stress symptoms (e.g., yellowing, wilting) that do not improve with proper irrigation.", "claims": ["supported: The recommended irrigation depth per application for sugarcane is 7–8 cm"], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "**Observation:**  \n- The agricultural knowledge states that the recommended irrigation depth per application for sugarcane is **7–8 cm**.\n\n**Analysis:**  \n- This indicates that each time you irrigate the sugarcane field, you should aim to apply water to a depth of 7 to 8 cm to meet the crop’s water requirement.\n\n**Confidence:**  \n- **High** – the value comes directly from the provided agricultural guidelines.\n\n**Recommendations:**  \n\n- **Immediate actions**  \n  - Apply water so that the soil receives a depth of **7–8 cm** in each irrigation event.\n\n- **Monitoring advice**  \n  - After irrigation, observe the soil‑moisture sensor to confirm that moisture has increased appropriately.  \n  - Keep an eye on leaf colour and turgor; normal green, firm leaves suggest adequate water.\n\n- **When to seek expert help**  \n  - If soil‑moisture readings stay unusually low or high despite applying the recommended depth.  \n  - If the crop shows persistent stress symptoms (e.g., yellowing, wilting) that do not improve with proper irrigation.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 0.68, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 198, "compl